 transcriptional generation (p300-mediated) and nuclear export (XPO1-mediated) of oncogenic factors. This combination achieved superior tumor suppression in vivo compared to monotherapy. CONCLUSION: Our findings position p300 as a central architect of pathogenic chromatin activation in MM. The combination of HAT inhibition (A485) and nuclear export inhibition (KPT8602) represents a novel, mechanistically rationalized therapeutic strategy to overcome epigenetic plasticity in MM.\n\n",
