ay integrated fluidic circuits (IFC) and BioMark HD Real-Time PCR system, which enabled efficient and precise analysis of gene expression patterns. Results were analyzed using Fluidigm's Real-Time PCR Analysis software and 2(-DeltaDeltaCt) formula was used for the calculation of expression changes. Notably, expression levels of INS, TMEM74 and IFNA2 genes were identified to be prominently altered in BCC comparted to adjacent healthy tissues. However, only IFNA2 expression showed statistically significant change in BCC. Consequently, these findings suggest that IFNA2 might play significant role in the regulation of autophagy in BCC development and progression and can be therapeutically targeted.\n\n",
